  "name": "cs142-proj1",
  "description": "A C++11 text-based hypertext browser implementation designed to parse and render documents containing embedded link metadata and navigable references. It utilizes a custom lexical scanner to tokenize input streams into discrete word objects and link destinations, storing document state in a tuple-based indexing structure to facilitate efficient reflow. The architecture incorporates a custom template-based option type for safe optional handling and an environment-configurable logging system for diagnostic tracing.",
